plit transform is installed, the host view’s frame is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"transformed bounding box, so each pass applies the layout fraction to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"picture a SECOND time — the content renders at fraction² of its box — and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"drifts the picture out of the frozen content mask, exposing black regions"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inside the box. react-native-video is immune: its layout stamps sublayers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bounds"},{"text":", which a transform never changes.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The lock captures the healthy pre-transform frame at acquisition and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"re-asserts it (through the host’s own frame API, via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restamp"},{"type":"text","text":") whenever"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the surface’s layer geometry deviates. Observed on the LAYER: UIView"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"geometry setters are not KVO-compliant, CALayer’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bounds"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"position"},{"type":"text","text":" are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"— the same technique as the overlay host view’s host-layer observers."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Construct on the main thread (it reads and may re-stamp view geometry);","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"release"},{"text":" only invalidates the observations and is safe from any thread.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"title":"ContentLayoutLock","externalID":"s:18OptiViewAdsRuntime17ContentLayoutLockC","roleHeading":"Class","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"}